BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  # The Myth of the River of Abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The River of Abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ance had a sacred property: any gift thrown into its waters would triple before reaching the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     other side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  The first village chose a Sender each moon to receive five golden seeds from the earth. The Se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    nder could plant them in home soil or cast them across the river. When seeds crossed the wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ers, they multiplied to fifteen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The receiving village would then choose how many seeds to return across the river's flowing ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    gic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  At first, the villages were cautious. Senders kept their seeds close, fearing betrayal. The vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    llages remained poor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  But one wise Sender trusted completely, casting all five seeds into the river. The Receiver, m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    oved by this faith, returned half the blessed harvest. Both villages prospered beyond what e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    ither could achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  Over generations, those who embraced the river's gift-trusting in the flow and honoring recipr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ocity-built abundant stores. Those who hoarded seeds in fear watched them wither.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
