BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      # The Myth of the River of Abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The River of A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        bundance had a sacred property: any gift thrown into its waters would triple before reac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        hing the other side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      The first village chose a Sender each moon to receive five golden seeds from the earth. Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        e Sender could plant them in home soil or cast them across the river. When seeds crossed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (         the waters, they multiplied to fifteen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The receiving village would then choose how many seeds to return across the river's flowin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        g magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      At first, the villages were cautious. Senders kept their seeds close, fearing betrayal. Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        e villages remained poor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      But one wise Sender trusted completely, casting all five seeds into the river. The Receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        r, moved by this faith, returned half the blessed harvest. Both villages prospered beyon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        d what either could achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      Over generations, those who embraced the river's gift-trusting in the flow and honoring re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        ciprocity-built abundant stores. Those who hoarded seeds in fear watched them wither.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      The elders taught: "The river multiplies what is given, but only trust and fair return cre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        ate lasting wealth. One hand extended requires another reaching back, for the sacred wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        ers bless the generous, not the grasping.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      # The Tale of the River and the Rain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      In the ancient days, the River spoke to the Rain, saying, "Share your waters with me, and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        I shall carry them to the distant sea.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      The Rain was fearful. "If I give you my waters, what shall remain for me?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      But the River replied, "Trust. For what you give shall return threefold.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      The Rain released a small offering. As the waters flowed through the River's channels, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        y nourished the valley below. Trees grew tall, their leaves reaching skyward. When the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        un warmed the earth, the waters rose again as mist, rejoining the Rain in the clouds - b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        ut now enriched threefold with the essence of the forest.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      The Rain sent more. The River, grateful for this trust, ensured the waters touched every f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ield and village. Each drop that fell returned multiplied, carrying the prayers of the p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        eople and the fragrance of blooming flowers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      Thus the cycle continued: each giving generously, each receiving abundantly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      The ancient ones taught: *What flows between two hearts grows larger than what either coul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        d hold alone. Trust sent downstream returns as blessing from above. The one who shares t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        he first drop makes the rain possible for all.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
